## Module 26 — Workforce Structures (Org Design)
**Oracle Equivalent:** Oracle Global HR — Workforce Structures

### NexusAI Pages Currently Existing
- ✅ [OrgChart.tsx](file:///Users/mbjunaid/My%20Projects/nexusai-erp-2/src/pages/OrgChart.tsx)
- ✅ [EmployeeDirectory.tsx](file:///Users/mbjunaid/My%20Projects/nexusai-erp-2/src/pages/EmployeeDirectory.tsx)
- ✅ Schema: [hr_structures.ts](file:///Users/mbjunaid/My%20Projects/nexusai-erp-2/shared/schema/hr_structures.ts) — Department, Location, Job, Position, Grade

### Oracle Pages/Forms NexusAI is Missing or Partial
| Oracle Form | NexusAI Status | Gap Description |
|---|---|---|
| **Geography Hierarchy** | ⚠️ Partial | Locations exist. Missing: Country → State → County → City validation hierarchy used for payroll tax and compliance. |
| **Job Families & Job Profiles** | ⚠️ Partial | Jobs exist. Missing: Job Family groupings and Job Profiles that attach required Competencies to a job. |
| **Grade Ladders (Pay Progression)** | ❌ Missing | Oracle defines step-based pay progression within Grades (e.g., Step 1: $50K, Step 2: $55K, Step 3: $60K). |
| **Establishment Reporting** | ❌ Missing | EEO-1 / VETS-4212 workforce demographic reporting required in the US for OFCCP compliance. |
| **Tree Versioning (Org Chart History)** | ❌ Missing | Oracle stores every previous state of the management hierarchy tree with effective dates. |
